NASTRAN-95 BASELINE QUALIFICATION
================================

Date:       2026-11-26
Source:     nasa/NASTRAN-95 @ 65e29e9db7b21a02bb42e723afa74fa7635ed765
Toolchain:  Debian bookworm, gfortran 12
Flags:      -std=legacy -fdec -fallow-invalid-boz -fno-automatic -O0
            -ffp-contract=off -fno-fast-math
            (strscn.f at -ffixed-line-length-72; others -none)

Policy
------
PASS       Normalized output identical to the 1995 demoout golden.
KNOWN_DIFF Same structure; numeric values within atol=1e-9 / rtol=1e-3.
MISSING    Deck needs an RSCARDS/INP1/SOF artifact not in the corpus.
RESTART    The 1995 output came from a checkpoint not in the corpus.
FAIL       Structural mismatch or numeric outside tolerance.

Results (132 decks)
-------------------
PASS        32
KNOWN_DIFF  32
MISSING     11
RESTART      8
FAIL        49

Qualified corpus: 64 decks (PASS + KNOWN_DIFF).

Residual categories
-------------------
The 49 FAILs are not parser failures. They are:
  - 10 superelement decks (d0202*) whose goldens include multi-phase/SOF
    output the single-run corpus does not provide.
  - ~12 decks where the solver took a different iteration count
    (USER INFORMATION MESSAGE 3028), shifting the following table.
  - ~10 genuine numeric differences (aero/eigenvalue decks such as
    d10021a, d07011a, d14011a, d03031a).
  - ~19 presentation/label differences, including the Hollerith
    continuation bug (NUMBEROF STATIONS, vs NUMBER OF STATIONS) and
    missing OLD FEER / MKAERO2 diagnostic blocks.

Why not byte-exact against 1995
-------------------------------
The 1995 outputs were produced by Sun f77 on SPARC. Compiler/FPU
differences, Hollerith continuation behavior, and missing checkpoint/SOF
artifacts make byte-exact reproduction impossible for a subset of the
corpus. The rebuilt baseline is the oracle for Rust parity. The 1995
goldens remain a partial historical sanity check.

Rust parity gate
----------------
A module ticket may merge only when the rebuilt baseline and the Rust
build produce byte-identical normalized output for every deck that
exercises the module, and the reviewer approves the diff and report.

Reproduce
---------
  docker run --rm -v "$PWD:/work" nastran-rs-build scripts/build-baseline.sh
  docker run --rm -v "$PWD:/work" nastran-rs-build python3 parity/run_all.py
  docker run --rm -v "$PWD:/work" nastran-rs-build python3 parity/qualify.py
